5. WIRING -- a self-test nothing runs is not a guard
================================================================================
`scripts/check-doc-l10n-selftest.py` already existed (51 cases) and NOTHING
invoked it: `rg -n "selftest" .github/workflows/*.yml scripts/*.sh` returned no
hits. Both self-tests are now wired:

* .github/workflows/ci.yml, `docs-l10n` job -> new "guard self-tests" step:
  `l10n-guard-selftest.py`, `check-doc-l10n-selftest.py`, and
  `bash scripts/l10n-guard.sh --before HEAD --after HEAD --report "$RUNNER_TEMP/l10n"`
  (the last walks the real 393-file tree, so a construct that parses on Linux
  CI but dies on bash 3.2 has somewhere to fail).
* scripts/verify-in-docker.sh -> new gate
  "localization guard self-tests: python3 scripts/l10n-guard-selftest.py &&
  python3 scripts/check-doc-l10n-selftest.py".

Both self-tests are green locally, including the previously unwired one:
  51/51 self-test case(s) passed        (before §7 added its case; 52/52 after)

Guards re-run after all edits:
  $ python3 -c "import yaml; yaml.safe_load(open('.github/workflows/ci.yml'))"   -> YAML_OK
  $ python3 scripts/ci/check-workflow-shells.py .github/workflows/ci.yml          -> OK
  $ python3 scripts/ci/check-script-portability.py                                -> OK (23 shell script(s))
  $ bash scripts/l10n-guard.sh --before HEAD --after HEAD --report ...            -> OK — L10n Guard: PASS

Portability work in the same edit: `is_excluded` expanded `"${EXCLUDE[@]}"`
under `set -u`, which is an unbound expansion on the bash 3.2 macOS still
ships; now `${EXCLUDE[@]+"${EXCLUDE[@]}"}`. No `mapfile`/`realpath`/`grep -P`/
`xargs -r` was introduced (portability gate above is the check).

