6. COVERAGE LIMITS (what this does NOT prove)
================================================================================
* The move test is content-based on whole trimmed lines. A translation that
  rewraps or rewords a sentence while moving it scores as a loss, not a move --
  deliberately conservative: it fails loudly rather than guessing.
* `removed-recorded.txt` trusts the reason text. Nothing here verifies prose in
  a Chinese sentence; the guard only forces a reason to exist and refuses
  entries without one (self-test `allow_list_without_reason_fails`). A wrong
  reason is a review problem, and the allow list is 3 lines, all of which were
  checked against the code in §2.
* No browser/terminal surface was touched by this change, so the standing
  browser-verification rule has no UI to exercise here; verification was the
  self-test suite, the three mutations, the real-tree guard run, and the
  pager/CLI test suites.
* The guard still only reads `crates/**/*.rs`. Markdown is `check-doc-l10n.py`'s
  job; that asymmetry is unchanged and documented in the skill.

